From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:55:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-jpeg: fix the end of DHT parsing and bound
 jpeg_skip()

jpeg_parse_huffman_tables() subtracts the two length bytes from len
before its loop, but ends with jpeg_skip(stream, len - 2). For every
well-formed DHT segment len is 0 there, so it asks to skip -2 bytes.
The size_t wraps, stream->curr + len wraps to two bytes before the
current position, the bounds check passes, and parsing resumes on the
last two HUFFVAL bytes. Valid baseline tables never hold 0xff there, so
this goes unnoticed, but a table that ends in ff db makes the parser
take a DQT marker that is not there.

A table whose BITS count more symbols than the segment holds is not
rejected either: HUFFVAL is read from the following segments and the
loop leaves len negative, which again turns into a backwards skip, so
the bogus table can be accepted. jpeg_parse_quantization_tables() has the
same overrun for 16-bit tables (it only checks for 65 bytes left), and
it does not skip what is left of its segment at all, so trailing bytes
are scanned for markers. An APP14 "Adobe" segment shorter than 14
bytes (or any APP14 segment shorter than its length field) reaches
jpeg_skip() with a negative length the same way and is accepted, an
Adobe one with a transform flag read from the next segment.

Reject tables that overrun their segment, skip the remainder of DHT and
DQT segments with the right length, and make jpeg_skip() compare with
the bytes left instead of computing a pointer past the buffer, so a
negative length fails.

Well-formed files parse as before: for 1180 frames from libjpeg-turbo,
ffmpeg, PIL, ImageMagick, a Logitech C170 camera and hand-made files,
the result of
v4l2_jpeg_parse_header() is identical before and after, every offset,
length and field, with and without table arrays.

Same code as the upstream series "media: v4l2-jpeg: fix segment length
handling in the header parser" (3 patches, folded into one here).

Fixes: 50733b5b9102 ("media: add v4l2 JPEG helpers")
Fixes: b8035f7988a8 ("media: Add parsing for APP14 data segment in jpeg helpers")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
index 36a0f1a1b..0258abdfb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
@@ -203,7 +203,12 @@ static int jpeg_get_word_be(struct jpeg_stream *stream)
 
 static int jpeg_skip(struct jpeg_stream *stream, size_t len)
 {
-	if (stream->curr + len > stream->end)
+	/*
+	 * Callers compute lengths as int: a negative one becomes a huge size_t
+	 * here. Compare with the bytes left, so the pointer addition can
+	 * neither wrap nor move backwards.
+	 */
+	if (len > (size_t)(stream->end - stream->curr))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	stream->curr += len;
@@ -447,6 +452,9 @@ static int jpeg_parse_quantization_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 		 */
 		if (pq != 0 && (pq != 1 || precision != 12))
 			return -EINVAL;
+		/* the table must fit in the segment */
+		if (len < (pq ? 129 : 65))
+			return -EINVAL;
 
 		/* quantization table destination identifier */
 		tq = pq_tq & 0xf;
@@ -467,7 +475,8 @@ static int jpeg_parse_quantization_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 		len -= pq ? 129 : 65;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/* Skip what is left of the segment, as for the other segments. */
+	return jpeg_skip(stream, len);
 }
 
 /* B.2.4.2 Huffman table-specification syntax */
@@ -514,6 +523,9 @@ static int jpeg_parse_huffman_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 
 			mt += li;
 		}
+		/* Tc/Th, BITS and HUFFVAL must fit in the segment */
+		if (17 + mt > len)
+			return -EINVAL;
 		/* HUFFVAL - values associated with each Huffman code */
 		ret = jpeg_skip(stream, mt);
 		if (ret < 0)
@@ -525,7 +537,8 @@ static int jpeg_parse_huffman_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 		}
 	}
 
-	return jpeg_skip(stream, len - 2);
+	/* len no longer includes the length field itself. */
+	return jpeg_skip(stream, len);
 }
 
 /* B.2.4.4 Restart interval definition syntax */
-- 
2.55.0

